        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(media): normalize case-insensitive file:// URI schemes in MEDIA directives (#103473)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\nclose #103473 \r\nURI schemes are case-insensitive per RFC 3986 §3.1, but `normalizeMediaSource()` used a case-sensitive `startsWith(\"file://\")` check, causing uppercase variants like `FILE://` or `File://` in `MEDIA:` directives to be passed through without stripping the scheme prefix. Local file paths wrapped in uppercase file URIs were not recognized correctly downstream.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n**Test results** — 59 tests pass, including 2 new cases for uppercase/mixed-case FILE://:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ corepack pnpm test src/media/parse.test.ts\r\n RUN  v4.1.9\r\n\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  59 passed (59)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Code change** (2 files, +7/−2 lines):\r\n\r\n`src/media/parse.ts` — scheme comparison is now case-insensitive:\r\n```ts\r\n- return src.startsWith(\"file://\") ? src.replace(\"file://\", \"\") : src;\r\n+ return src.toLowerCase().startsWith(\"file://\") ? src.slice(7) : src;\r\n```\r\n\r\n`src/media/parse.test.ts` — 2 new test cases:\r\n```ts\r\n[\"/tmp/generated.png\", \"MEDIA:FILE:///tmp/generated.png\"],\r\n[\"/tmp/generated.png\", \"MEDIA:File:///tmp/generated.png\"],\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Build verification** — dist output confirmed to contain the fix:\r\n```\r\n✓ Fix confirmed in dist/payloads-HhftmjTZ.js\r\n✓ All test cases passed (function logic verified in build output)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Format and lint** — clean.\r\n",
